{{Story head|[[Theresis]] faces [[Priestess]] in the [[Assimilated Universe]] and wrestles partial control of [[Originium]] from her. Badly harmed by the efforts of Theresis and [[Theresa]], Priestess fell into slumber, but now she has awoken.}}
{{sc|1|mode=background}}
{{sc|When 'she' awakens<br/>[[Assimilated Universe]]|mode=subtitle}}
{{sc|The sea rolls quietly.|mode=action}}
{{sc|[[Theresis]] falls in the ocean of information. The massive quantity buffets him, assimilating his cognition.<br/>He can feel his mind grow slow, but he still tries to follow the guidance left behind by [[Theresa]]—<br/>Guided by his sword, the information flow reconstructed by Theresa clashes with the preexisting one.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|The waves splash violently.|mode=action}}
{{sc|The massive collision lasts only an instant.<br/>The surface begins to surge. Then, the sea splits open, as if sliced by a sharp blade.<br/>A dark abyss appears in the Assimilated Universe. The sea of data stirs and roils.<br/>Waves crashing against waves, drowning out one another.<br/>Even as his mind grows numb, Theresis can sense the will gazing upon him weaken rapidly.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Theresis|Your plan worked, Theresa.<br/>Sever their control over Amnannam and seize it—}}
{{sc|But suddenly, all the violent scenes come to a screeching halt.<br/>She opens her eyes and sees the small, frail creature.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|???|(Unknown language) Connection... unstable.<br/>(Unknown language) —It's you?}}
{{sc|2|mode=background}}
{{sc|Calm Voice|(Unknown language) Your actions surprise me.<br/>(Unknown language) ...'Theresa' and 'Theresis'.}}
{{sc|Theresis does not comprehend the space before him. Perhaps it is simply another illusion of a dying mind—<br/>Until he hears a familiar language that he can understand.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Calm Voice|Ah, but perhaps this was the result that one wanted to see?<br/>Your intentions are as easy to decipher as your language.<br/>The evolution of [[Terra]] had brought many surprises... a shame.}}
{{sc|Theresis approaches.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Theresis|You think we failed.<br/>Then why do you hide and refuse to show yourself?}}
{{sc|He meditatively swings his sword, guiding the chaotic information through the pure-white space...|mode=speech}}
{{sc|He shatters the empty space into pieces.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Theresis|Falsehoods.}}
{{sc|60_i23|mode=image}}
{{sc|Priestess|You've implemented a backdoor in my project and restricted my access.<br/>The data tells me I'm losing this piece of [[Originium]]. My attempts at maintenance have been in vain.<br/>Impressive. Your rash actions have borne fruit.}}
{{sc|There is nothing physically imposing to the voice whispering about failure before Theresis.<br/>But this simply serves to make him more wary.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Theresis|Your arrogance reminds me of someone.<br/>[[Doctor|Someone who deceived me]]. There is more than one [[Predecessor|evil spirit of a bygone age]].}}
{{sc|Priestess|Dr. {nickname}... I see you've met.<br/>Then let me introduce myself.<br/>[[Priestess]]. Linguist, and colleague to Dr. {nickname}.}}
{{sc|Theresis cannot care less who Priestess is.<br/>Priestess or evil spirit, it makes no difference to him.<br/>He clutches his sword tightly. He will find a way to break through.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Priestess|You are anxious to defy a reality that you cannot perceive, Theresis.<br/>You were much calmer when you plotted with {nickname} on the border of [[Kazdel]].}}
{{sc|Theresis|You were watching...}}
{{sc|Priestess|Watching? No.<br/>I have long lost the energy and passion to observe the evolution of a newborn civilization.<br/>All I did was look up the data newly added to Originium, and checked some information that interested me.<br/>The expansion of Originium is a consensus between me and {nickname}.<br/>The current circumstances of Terra have somewhat differed from our predictions, but it remains on track.<br/>I admit to being surprised by your attempt to retake this Originium, but the duty of it will be fulfilled, no matter how you struggle.}}
{{sc|Theresis|You can believe what you want, creator of Originium.<br/>You believe that Originium is immovable, but she opened a path here, and liberated the myriad souls.<br/>She was not the first to resist, and I will not be the last. Someone will stand before you—<br/>Until there is none left to toy with our fate.}}
{{sc|Priestess|'Fate'... do you continue to believe that Originium stands opposed to the fate of your civilization?<br/>If you truly understand the history of your people, have you ever questioned why you have evolved in our likeness?}}
{{sc|Theresis|......}}
{{sc|Priestess|You do not understand what you are resisting.}}
{{sc|Theresis observes his surroundings. He is certain that he is still inside Originium.<br/>The nature of what makes up this place is no different from the tower that Theresa weaved—it is information reconstructed.<br/>Theresa has left him the key. He is sure he can put an end to this enigma.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Priestess|You noticed.}}
{{sc|Theresis|You do not have a real physical form. We're still in that ocean.}}
{{sc|Priestess|In the language of Originium, reality and falsehood are not polar opposites.<br/>When I first created this language, I wanted it to decipher the ultimate question that we had been unable to answer, despite all our efforts.<br/><i>It.</i><br/>{nickname} once had hope for the beings on this land... guiding them to evolve and seek hope through Originium, giving them a chance to face It, perhaps even overcome It.<br/>But they are doomed to despair.<br/>'[[Teekaz]]'. You were not part of the plan, but you became the species most affected by Originium. An accident.<br/>I must applaud your courage for standing here.}}
{{sc|Theresis|An accident...? Is this how you summarize our fate?<br/>You're certainly alike, Priestess.<br/>You call the fates you toy with a gift of hope, millennia of suffering a necessary sacrifice.<br/>But {nickname} was honest, at least.}}
{{sc|Theresis swings his sword.|mode=action}}
{{sc|His sword pierces falsehood, but the space on the other side—|mode=speech}}
{{sc|2|mode=background}}
{{sc|Theresis|Nothing changed?}}
{{sc|Theresis closes his eyes and raises his sword.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Priestess|Your violence is meaningless.}}
{{sc|Theresis|If you didn't care whether this pathetic race of mine can seize its own fate, you should have eliminated me already.<br/>You're still weak after awakening from a long dream, are you not, Presence?{{sic|Priestess}}}}
{{sc|SLASH!|mode=action}}
{{sc|He lunges without hesitation.<br/>The sword-wave cuts through the figure, disappearing without a sound into the pale white wall in the distance.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Priestess|I said, this is meaningless.}}
{{sc|SLASH!|mode=action}}
{{sc|Another strike.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Theresis|I've always wondered—what exactly is the difference between you, the self-proclaimed creators, and us?}}
{{sc|Theresis repeatedly attacks with his sword.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Theresis holds nothing back. The white wall begins to crack.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Theresis|You have not brought everything to a standstill.<br/>You just wanted to buy more time, or simply to mock the struggles of a pathetic race...<br/>Suit yourself, Priestess.}}
{{sc|shakes|mode=background}}
{{sc|Once again, Theresis senses the surging tide of information, remnants of the broken tower that Theresa weaved.<br/>Theresis swings again.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|SLASH!|mode=action}}
{{sc|Golden seawater shatters the pale wall, rushing into this seemingly boundless white space.<br/>The tide swallows all that it sees, but parts before the figure of Priestess...<br/>Like a static comet, leaving behind a black tail of calm in the sea of surging fury.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Theresis|Your connection to the Originium is weakening. You are fading away.}}
{{sc|Priestess|Continuing to process this disorganized data is a waste of energy.}}
{{sc|The waves converge upon the last area, slowly submerging Priestess's figure.<br/>They also close in upon Theresis.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Priestess|Is this the end that you sought?<br/>The [[Sarkaz]] data has corrupted part of the Assimilated Universe. The data has been deleted, but I do not have time right now to repair the rewritten structures.<br/>You can 'survive' in the Assimilated Universe in another form.}}
{{sc|Theresis|Survive?<br/>I came to pass judgment upon the gods.}}
{{sc|The Sarkaz swings his sword at the creator one last time, before the torrent of information engulfs him.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|SLASH!|mode=action}}
{{sc|Alarms blaring|mode=action}}
{{sc|Warning.<br/>Unknown threat.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|fades out|mode=background}}
{{sc|HE-The Law|mode=image}}
{{sc|Mechanical whirring|mode=action}}
{{sc|Identifying error code... identification failed.<br/>Simulating path... simulation failed.<br/>Rebooting bottom-level computing area...<br/>Assessing danger level...<br/>Repeat.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Yvangelista XI|And there I was, thinking that all I had to do—after I find a successor—was hand out candies to the children.<br/>......<br/>You have never proclaimed such a revelation before.}}
{{sc|Hall of Stasis|mode=backgroundimg}}
{{sc|Static crackling|mode=action}}
{{sc|'Preserver'|(Unknown language) Incoming data... Originium...<br/>(Unknown language) A warning, or yet another swan song of hope?<br/>(Unknown language) Where are you, kindred? What have you encountered?}}
{{sc|Hall of Stasis Activated|mode=backgroundimg}}
{{sc|'Preserver'|......}}
{{sc|3|mode=background}}
{{sc|Flames crackling|mode=action}}
{{sc|Witch King|......}}
{{sc|The wind brushes past the throne. The sovereign's gaze moves away from the depths of the void outside his domain.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Witch King|This music exists outside of order. How did it invade my Pavillon, my Leithanien?<br/>The traces of genesis?<br/>......}}
{{sc|Black|mode=background}}
{{sc|Waves crashing|mode=action}}
{{sc|Silence is broken.<br/>Priestess's figure, shattered by the golden waves of information, disappears without a trace.<br/>The sea of data dashes against Theresis even more furiously.<br/>His mind grows crowded. His body begins to crack.<br/>The waves of information take away the blood that flows from his wounds. Originium crystals multiply in every cell...|mode=speech}}
{{sc|He sinks deeper into the sea.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Theresis is completely inundated.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|1|mode=background}}
{{sc|Blood-red seawater gushes from the bottomless abyss, melting into the golden sea.<br/>The sea of data in the Assimilated Universe turns a dark red, like blood, the color of the Sarkaz.<br/>Finally, a tiny figure rises from the sea.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Weak Voice|We took control of Amnannam, Theresa.<br/>I can feel the direction that the waves flow now, and the massive amounts of data that I cannot comprehend—}}
{{sc|He wants to share his joy, but there is only the sound of the waves in the boundless void.<br/>He can no longer hear even his own heartbeat. There is only him here.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Half of Theresis's body is now completely covered in Originium crystals.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Theresis|......}}
{{sc|There is no longer any meaning in staying here.<br/>He will return alone to Terra, to the land that belongs to him—|mode=speech}}
{{sc|The rhombus in the void grows faint and broken...<br/>Priestess's consciousness once again falls into slumber.<br/>The spread of Originium has been far slower than expected, and she has unexpectedly lost part of her control over it.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Priestess|Two Terrans, a frail and overlooked race.<br/>I'm starting to understand why you're so interested in them... {nickname}.}}
{{sc|As her consciousness fades into darkness, she turns her gaze to the land known as Terra...<br/>She sees the one they call [[Doctor]] walking with [[Amiya|the Cautus]] and [[Kal'tsit|AMa-10]] into the dark passage that leads to the underground throne room—<br/>She sees the city of [[Londinium]] cry out in pain in the fires of war—<br/>...She sees death—<br/>[[Hierda|A disintegrating Cautus]], whose information is melting into the Assimilated Universe's sea of data—<br/>Then, she reaches out.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|4|mode=background}}
{{sc|Raydistorter|(Unknown language) And that was the last time you saw Priestess?}}
{{sc|Hierda|(Unknown language) Yes.<br/>(Unknown language) I still have many unanswered questions. Time is no longer my major concern.}}
{{sc|Raydistorter|(Unknown language) Do you not miss your home, traveler?}}
{{sc|Hierda|......}}
{{sc|'Miss.'<br/>—The Cautus answered this question many times when she lived on the ship that housed the gods.<br/>There is no future in the fragments of time reconstructed from information.<br/>Her best friends soon forget her existence entirely.<br/>She can know all there it is to them, but she will never truly be part of life here.<br/>'I'm just a traveler lucky enough to catch a glimpse of the distant past.'|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Hierda|(Unknown language) I'm having another learning session with Presence.<br/>(Unknown language) Are you sure you don't want to come and talk to her?}}
{{sc|Raydistorter|(Unknown language) You seem eager to resolve our conflict, Hierda, but I'm afraid I must decline.}}
{{sc|They will not change.<br/>They are simply recreations of data.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Hierda|......<br/>(Unknown language) Very well.}}
{{sc|The Cautus looks out beyond the porthole and counts silently. When the count reaches thirty, life from the star will once again shine upon the surface of the broken planet.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Hierda|It's breath-taking, no matter how many times I see it...<br/>Life and death emerging at the same time—}}
{{sc|A scene that she had never seen on that land. A scene that she does not wish her brethren to see.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|"Farewell. I'm leaving."|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Hierda|—?!}}
{{sc|5|mode=background}}
{{sc|In the blink of an eye, the Cautus finds herself back on that pale soil.<br/>Priestess welcomes her with a smile.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Priestess slowly approaches.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Priestess|Have you found your answer?}}
{{sc|The Cautus shakes her head.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Hierda|Where are you going?}}
{{sc|Priestess|Terra. Your home.}}
{{sc|Hierda|—?!}}
{{sc|Priestess|I want to give you a choice, [[Hierda]].<br/>You can stay, learn the knowledge that you thirst for, and find answers to the questions in your heart.<br/>Or, I can send you back home.}}
{{sc|Hierda|Home...? To Terra?!}}
{{sc|Priestess|However, it may mean forsaking forever the chance to find those answers.<br/>What's more, you will find that you have become very different from your erstwhile kin. It will bring you even more pain.<br/>I will respect your decision, Hierda.}}
{{sc|Hierda|I, I—}}
{{sc|White|mode=background}}
{{sc|At the same time, you step into the space within the rift.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|6|mode=background}}
{{sc|The wind blows quietly.|mode=action}}
{{sc|Doctor|This place...<br/>It's not the Abyss...}}
{{sc|Mon3tr|(Angry roar)}}
{{sc|Amiya|Did [[PRTS]] bring us out here?}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|It's not that simple. We are the only ones here.}}
{{sc|The deck is completely silent.<br/>You turn around and notice the absence of the [[Elite Op|elite operators]] and [[Ascalon]]—|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Doctor|Black... rain?}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|No. Massive amounts of Originium dust. Protect yourself.<br/>Protect the Doctor, [[Mon3tr]].}}
{{sc|Originium crystals spread across the floor.|mode=action}}
{{sc|7|mode=background}}
{{sc|Amiya|Dr. [[Kal'tsit]]! Beneath our feet!<br/>The deck is crystallizing rapidly. At this rate...}}
{{sc|Black Originium dust accumulates on the deck. Tiny Originium clusters grow like wild grass.<br/>You can see them spreading as far as one's eyes can reach, gleaming enchantingly in the sun.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Kal'tsit|Warn all operators still on Rhodes Island to be prepared for [[Catastrophe]], Amiya.}}
{{sc|Amiya|Understood.<br/>I'm not getting through! All communications have failed—}}
{{sc|Doctor|It's too quiet.}}
{{sc|The sight before you is inconceivable, different from any Catastrophe that you have witnessed before.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Doctor|The Originium expands at an impossible pace.}}
{{sc|You look down at the deck, now completely covered in Originium, and see only your shadow.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Doctor|......}}
{{sc|Amiya|Doctor—}}
{{sc|You turn around to see a stunned look on Kal'tsit's face.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Doctor|...Kal'tsit?}}
{{sc|The Prelude A|mode=image}}
{{sc|60_i24_2|mode=image}}
{{sc|You follow her gaze. Far in the distance on the deck, a small formation of black Originium is growing slowly towards the sky.<br/>You see a faint white figure on every facet of the crystal.<br/>A figure not unfamiliar to you—<br/>The black Originium rain suddenly grows more intense.<br/>It almost feels like the large black raindrops are not falling from the sky, but rushing from the ground towards the heavens.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|60_i24_3|mode=image}}
{{sc|They refract the sunlight, drawing colorful lines in the sky—<br/>All the colors you see begin to converge and weave into a white curtain, glistening with rainbow colors, slowly descending.<br/>A pure, pristine white, gentle draping over the Originium crystal on the deck—|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Doctor|Crystal...}}
{{sc|60_i24_4|mode=image}}
{{sc|A beautiful figure stands upon the crystal.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|60_i24_5|mode=image}}
{{sc|Black crystal retreats from her legs, and white light puts a layer of clothing on her.<br/>Heaven and earth, white and black, and—|mode=speech}}
{{sc|Doctor|...... / Priestess.}}
{{sc|She looks upon the land that has long become unfamiliar to her.|mode=speech}}
{{sc|60_i25|mode=image}}
{{sc|Priestess|Long time no see.}}
